  "worked_solution": "To find the complex conjugate, we flip the sign of the imaginary part.\n\nIn the given number $z=-\\frac{1}{2}i,$ the imaginary part is $-\\frac{1}{2}i$ (there is no real part, just an imaginary part). Flipping the sign, we get $\\frac{1}{2}i.$\n\nTherefore, the complex conjugate is given by $\\overset{\u2015}{z}=\\frac{1}{2}i.$",
